  * -- Overview
Refactors gomarkdown and gousage to use struct-based flag registration. Both tools now write an output file only when its contents would change.

  * -- Key Changes
cmd/gomarkdown
  * Replaced package-level flag variables and init() registration with a cmdlineFlags struct registered via flags.RegisterFlagsInStruct.
  * Moved --markdown and --gopkg validation into cmdlineFlags.validate(), which now runs before the package locator.
  * Split main into smaller helpers: generateMarkdown, mergePackages, markdownForPackage, packageDoc, fallbackPackageDoc and allExamples.
  * Moved the cgo/build-cache fallback parsing into its own function, fallbackPackageDoc.
  * writeMarkdown skips files whose contents are unchanged and prints updated: <file> only for files it actually writes. It replaces writeAllowed.

cmd/gousage
  * Same struct-based flag registration (--go-output, --overwrite).
  * writeGo compares the gofmt'd output with the existing file, skips the write if they match, and prints updated: <file> only on write. It replaces writeAllowed.

Both
  * Fixed the "overwite" typo in the overwrite error message.

  * -- Breaking Changes
None to flags or their defaults. Behaviour changes:
  * Without --overwrite, an existing file with identical contents is now a silent success instead of an error.
  * The stdout message changes from writing: <file> (printed for every file) to updated: <file> (printed only for changed files).

